# Koh, the Face Stealer (CR 607.2a, 607.5, 613.1f): Koh's enters trigger exiles Bot2's Emperor of Bones on turn 3, and on turn 5 Bot1
# pays 1 life to choose it. Koh then has the Emperor's three abilities, linked to one another on Koh but not to Koh's own: at the
# beginning of combat the granted trigger exiles the Llanowar Elves Bot2's Shock killed, and the granted adapt puts two +1/+1
# counters on Koh, so the granted "put a creature card exiled with this creature onto the battlefield" finds the Elves (the lone
# card that ability's partner exiled, no question) and not the Emperor, which Koh's own ability exiled and stays in exile.

